<!doctype html><html lang="en" dir="ltr" data-theme="kujo-light"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/presentation/favicon.svg"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Overview — KUJO — Trust at the speed of AI.</title><meta name="description" content="18-slide investor briefing with source evidence, recorded execution and editable planning assumptions."><link rel="canonical" href="https://invest.kujolang.ai/overview/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="KUJO — Trust at the speed of AI."><meta property="og:description" content="18-slide investor briefing with source evidence, recorded execution and editable planning assumptions."><meta name="twitter:title" content="KUJO — Trust at the speed of AI."><meta name="twitter:description" content="18-slide investor briefing with source evidence, recorded execution and editable planning assumptions."><meta property="og:url" content="https://invest.kujolang.ai/overview/"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","description":"18-slide investor briefing with source evidence, recorded execution and editable planning assumptions.","inLanguage":"en","name":"KUJO — Trust at the speed of AI.","url":"https://invest.kujolang.ai/overview/"}</script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/sitekit/sitekit.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/presentation/presentation.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/deck/theme.css"><meta property="og:image" content="https://invest.kujolang.ai/assets/deck/social/overview.f2e3f1b36e7d.png"><meta property="og:image:secure_url" content="https://invest.kujolang.ai/assets/deck/social/overview.f2e3f1b36e7d.png"><meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png"><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"><meta property="og:image:height" content="630"><meta property="og:image:alt" content="KUJO — Investor overview. 18 slides. Trust at the speed of AI."><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://invest.kujolang.ai/assets/deck/social/overview.f2e3f1b36e7d.png"><meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="KUJO — Investor overview. 18 slides. Trust at the speed of AI."></head><body><a class="p-skip" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a><main id="main-content" class="p-overview sk-container"><header class="p-overview-header"><div><p class="p-kicker">KUJO / 18 slides</p><h1>KUJO — Trust at the speed of AI.</h1><p>18-slide investor briefing with source evidence, recorded execution and editable planning assumptions.</p></div><a class="sk-button" href="/">Start presentation ↗</a></header><div class="p-thumbnails sk-grid"><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-cover p-inverse"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>Investor briefing / November 2026</span><span dir="ltr">1 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Trust at the
speed of AI.</h1><p class="ki-lead">The programming language and accountability infrastructure for agent-driven development.</p><ol class="p-features"></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><img class="ki-mark" width="256" height="256" src="/assets/deck/kujo-logomark.svg" alt="Kujo"><div class="ki-wordmark">KUJO</div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span></span><span>1</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>1</span> Trust at the
speed of AI.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/2/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-split"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>02 / The accountability problem</span><span dir="ltr">2 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Software production is outpacing verification.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Agents can report completion. Teams still need a reviewable chain from requested work to release decision.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>The claim</h2><p>“Tests passed. Ready to merge.” An illustrative agent statement.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>The evidence</h2><p>Command, exit code, changed revision, environment and retained failure output.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>The gap</h2><p>Useful logs already exist. Connecting them across tools and review boundaries remains work.</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>Thesis · existing agent controls acknowledged</span><span>2</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>2</span> Software production is outpacing verification.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/3/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-flow"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>03 / Structural shift</span><span dir="ltr">3 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Greater autonomy requires stronger accountability.</h1><p class="ki-lead">The cost of an unverified action grows as agents gain authority.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>Suggest code</h2><p>Human selects the change → diff review</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>Complete a task</h2><p>Agent edits and runs commands → execution records</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>Operate a workflow</h2><p>Retries and external effects → boundaries, recovery and approval</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>Conceptual progression; not a measured adoption curve</span><span>3</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>3</span> Greater autonomy requires stronger accountability.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/4/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-metrics p-inverse"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>04 / Why now</span><span dir="ltr">4 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>AI use is broad. Trust remains conditional.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Adoption of AI assistance is not evidence of autonomous production deployment.</p><ol class="p-features"></ol><dl class="p-metrics"><div class="p-metric"><dt>use coding assistants or coding agents at work</dt><dd>65.9%</dd></div><div class="p-metric"><dt>use AI agents or automated workflows at work</dt><dd>26.2%</dd></div><div class="p-metric"><dt>trust AI when answers are easy to validate</dt><dd>48%</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>M03–M04 · Stack Overflow Developer Survey 2026</span><span>4</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>4</span> AI use is broad. Trust remains conditional.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/5/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-architecture"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>05 / The Kujo system</span><span dir="ltr">5 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Build with clarity. Operate with control.</h1><p class="ki-lead">The language is the long-term foundation. Existing tools offer an earlier route into engineering workflows.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>Clarity</h2><p>Kujo language / Spec / Eval: explicit intent and testable outcomes.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>Context</h2><p>MCP / CaseFile / RunLedger: useful inputs, debugging evidence and run records.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>Control</h2><p>Dispatch / Workcell / ShipCheck: orchestration, bounded execution and release checks.</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-foundation">Existing repositories + coding agents <span>explicit component contracts</span> Kujo runtime + CLI</div><div class="ki-explore"><details><summary>Inspect the execution boundary</summary><p>Workcell owns supported container bounds. Dispatch owns workflow state. Neither confers enterprise certification.</p></details><details><summary>Inspect the evidence boundary</summary><p>CaseFile captures commands. Eval runs configured checks. RunLedger stores supplied outcomes. Artifacts remain separate.</p></details></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>T01–T14 · tool boundaries remain distinct</span><span>5</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>5</span> Build with clarity. Operate with control.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/6/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-lifecycle"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>06 / Lifecycle</span><span dir="ltr">6 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Accountability spans the whole task.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Each component owns a specific responsibility. A reviewable workflow composes their artifacts explicitly.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>Instruction → Context</h2><p>Spec / PackWrite → MCP and repository context</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>Execution → Evaluation</h2><p>Dispatch / Workcell → Eval result artifacts</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>Evidence → Review → Release</h2><p>CaseFile / RunLedger → reviewer → ShipCheck gate</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-boundary">Human authority remains explicit at the release decision.</div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>Composition map; not automatic end-to-end enforcement</span><span>6</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>6</span> Accountability spans the whole task.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/7/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-split"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>07 / Engineering proof</span><span dir="ltr">7 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>The foundation is already being built.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Inspect the implementation and its limits, then reproduce the smallest useful proof.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>Language and VM</h2><p>Kujo 1.9.0 is documented; a local 1.9.0 binary executes the recorded fixture tooling.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>Bounded execution</h2><p>Workcell 1.3 documents Docker/Podman limits, explicit exports and receipt verification.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>Reviewable artifact</h2><p>This presentation uses the native Kujo builder. Its demo retains a failing command, correction and evaluation.</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>T01, T03, T08, T14 · release documentation ≠ all HEAD features</span><span>7</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>7</span> The foundation is already being built.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/8/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-demo"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>08 / Recorded demonstration</span><span dir="ltr">8 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>A claim becomes inspectable evidence.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Recorded local coding fixture: correct a post-money ownership calculation. Inspect what failed, what changed and what passed.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>Request</h2><p>Return 20% for $6M raised at $30M post-money.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>Execution</h2><p>CaseFile captures real Node assertion failure and corrected execution.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>Decision</h2><p>Eval checks the correction. Accept this fixture; no production release.</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-explore"><details><summary>Inspect the correction</summary><pre>− raise / (postMoney + raise) * 100
+ raise / postMoney * 100</pre><span href="/assets/deck/appendix#evidence">Open failure, commands & evaluation →</span></details></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>Assistant-authored seeded fixture · CaseFile + Eval · local host</span><span>8</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>8</span> A claim becomes inspectable evidence.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/9/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-flow"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>09 / Adoption without migration</span><span dir="ltr">9 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Adopt the ecosystem before the language.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Keep application code in its existing language. Introduce accountability at the workflow boundary.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>Today: wrap the task</h2><p>Use CaseFile for command evidence and Eval for explicit repository checks.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>Then: control execution</h2><p>Adopt Dispatch or Workcell after validating the target environment and runtime pins.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>Over time: go deeper</h2><p>Choose Kujo for new agent tooling where native language integration adds value.</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>T02–T04, T08 · tools have their own runtime dependencies</span><span>9</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>9</span> Adopt the ecosystem before the language.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/10/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-split"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>10 / Initial customer</span><span dir="ltr">10 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Start with teams already delegating engineering work.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Proposed beachhead: agent-platform builders shipping repeatable engineering workflows.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>Buyer / user</h2><p>Platform engineering lead / engineers operating coding-agent harnesses.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>Immediate pain</h2><p>Failed runs are expensive to reconstruct. Review spans commits, logs and agent transcripts.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>Purchase hypothesis</h2><p>Pay for retained evidence, controlled execution and team review if they reduce investigation time.</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>Proposed segment; no customer interviews or demand validation</span><span>10</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>10</span> Start with teams already delegating engineering work.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/11/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-flow"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>11 / Business model</span><span dir="ltr">11 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Open tooling can lead to a commercial operating layer.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Earn developer trust through useful local tools. Charge for shared operational responsibilities.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>Available foundation</h2><p>Open repositories and local developer tooling.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>Proposed team service</h2><p>Hosted evidence, retention, shared review and execution capacity.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>Proposed enterprise tier</h2><p>Organization policy, deployment controls, support and governance.</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>Hosted offerings and pricing are proposals, not available SKUs</span><span>11</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>11</span> Open tooling can lead to a commercial operating layer.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/12/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-metrics"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>12 / Market model</span><span dir="ltr">12 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>A focused entry market can support a meaningful business.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Illustrative bottom-up model. Organization counts and annual contracts are assumptions to validate.</p><ol class="p-features"></ol><dl class="p-metrics"><div class="p-metric"><dt>initial target organizations × $24K ACV</dt><dd>2,000</dd></div><div class="p-metric"><dt>illustrative annual serviceable revenue pool</dt><dd>$48M</dd></div><div class="p-metric"><dt>100 customers × $24K; milestone scenario, not forecast</dt><dd>$2.4M</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>Planning only · editable assumptions in appendix</span><span>12</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>12</span> A focused entry market can support a meaningful business.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/13/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-split"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>13 / Position and defensibility</span><span dir="ltr">13 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Accountability requires more than generating code.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Existing platforms are strong. Kujo must win on useful evidence and the cost of operating reliable workflows.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>Coding agents / GitHub</h2><p>Generation, repository context and review are already integrated into major developer surfaces.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>Orchestration / LangGraph</h2><p>Persistence, recovery and human review are established capabilities.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>Kujo opportunity</h2><p>Connect explicit contracts, bounded work and inspectable artifacts. Prove adoption before claiming a moat.</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>C01–C02, T01–T14 · no exclusivity or benchmark superiority</span><span>13</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>13</span> Accountability requires more than generating code.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/14/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-flow"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>14 / Distribution</span><span dir="ltr">14 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Meet developers inside their existing workflows.</h1><p class="ki-lead">The planned December 2026 open-source campaign should produce repeat usage and customer learning.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>Discovery</h2><p>GitHub releases, technical demos, docs and reproducible fixtures → qualified visits.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>Activation</h2><p>Agent harness recipes and MCP tooling → first successful evidence run.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>Retention → revenue</h2><p>Repeat weekly runs → design-partner discussions → paid pilots and renewal evidence.</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>Campaign and partnerships planned; measure cohorts, not raw impressions</span><span>14</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>14</span> Meet developers inside their existing workflows.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/15/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-split"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>15 / Momentum</span><span dir="ltr">15 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Execution is visible. Demand still needs proof.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Engineering output, external adoption and commercial traction are different measures.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>Engineering output</h2><p>Public repositories, documented releases and the locally reproduced evidence fixture.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>External adoption</h2><p>Verified outside usage, retention and independent integrations: data not supplied.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>Commercial traction</h2><p>Design partners, paying customers and revenue: data not supplied. Complete before investor distribution.</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>Unavailable is not zero; no invented traction</span><span>15</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>15</span> Execution is visible. Demand still needs proof.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/16/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-split"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>16 / Founder and team</span><span dir="ltr">16 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Built through sustained open-source engineering.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Robert DeVore connects open-web product work with a growing language and developer-tooling ecosystem.</p><ol class="p-features"><li><span class="p-feature-number">01</span><div><h2>Background</h2><p>Public biography describes years of WordPress, WooCommerce, plugins and publishing systems.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">02</span><div><h2>Current work</h2><p>Language/runtime infrastructure, orchestration, evaluation, telemetry and evidence workflows.</p></div></li><li><span class="p-feature-number">03</span><div><h2>Team enabled by capital</h2><p>Proposed hires in runtime, execution reliability and developer experience; later customer engineering.</p></div></li></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>F01 · first-person source; no invented tenure, team or security credentials</span><span>16</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>16</span> Built through sustained open-source engineering.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/17/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-funding p-inverse"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>17 / Investment and milestones</span><span dir="ltr">17 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Capital turns a technical foundation into an adopted platform.</h1><p class="ki-lead">Working seed scenario. Financing terms and hiring pace remain assumptions.</p><ol class="p-features"></ol><dl class="p-metrics"><div class="p-metric"><dt>target raise</dt><dd>$6M</dd></div><div class="p-metric"><dt>post-money valuation or SAFE cap assumption</dt><dd>$30M</dd></div><div class="p-metric"><dt>planned runway, including reserve</dt><dd>24 mo</dd></div></dl></div><div class="ki-milestones"><span>0–6 mo<br>Flagship evidence workflow</span><span>6–12 mo<br>External validation + pilots</span><span>12–24 mo<br>Paid retention + repeatability</span></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>20% simplified ownership before further dilution · $150K founder annual base</span><span>17</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>17</span> Capital turns a technical foundation into an adopted platform.</span></a><a class="p-thumbnail" href="/18/"><div class="p-frame" aria-hidden="true" inert><article class="p-canvas p-layout-ki-close p-inverse"><header class="p-header"><span>KUJO</span><span>18 / The vision</span><span dir="ltr">18 / 18</span></header><div class="ki-content"><h1>Agents will build more software.</h1><p class="ki-lead">The organizations deploying it will still be accountable for what it does.</p><ol class="p-features"></ol><dl class="p-metrics"></dl></div><div class="ki-closing">KUJO<br><small>Trust at the speed of AI.</small><span href="https://robertdevore.com/contact/">Investor conversations ↗</span></div><div class="ki-resource"><span href="/assets/deck/appendix">Evidence & investor appendix ↗</span></div><footer class="p-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><span>KUJO · Trust at the speed of AI.</span><span>18</span></footer></article></div><span class="p-thumbnail-label"><span>18</span> Agents will build more software.</span></a></div><footer class="p-overview-footer"><span>KUJO / Investor briefing</span><a href="/reading/">Read the complete deck as text →</a></footer></main><script type="module" src="https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js/vce701823e78c4301a35b7e07294d87301792088814092" integrity="sha512-UKNk8GbxkABxKcXYuLkO16EleLGUkcvJWtpSNmExE0Too3ZaFAxTscNWEc1OdAv5/BikHawapSCaiD2XCmp+Bw==" data-cf-beacon='{"version":"2024.11.0","token":"1d30a17a0e01472db240809ad42c0b1f","r":1,"spa":2}' crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
</body></html>